DISPOSITION
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
A complete, HIG-native SwiftUI BackupRestorePage shipped at parity with the web source: a
pure @Observable state holder (ADR-004 — no networking in the view) exposing loading/empty/
error/success for BOTH feeds (configs, runs) over an injectable BackupRestoreDataSource seam,
with derived stats (totalConfigs/totalBackups/lastBackup/totalSize), the create/edit modal
(dynamic per-provider settings), delete confirmation, restore preview (checksum + metadata +
tables), trigger / quick-backup / verify / download actions, and the recent-errors callout.
The page reproduces the web chrome (title/subtitle + Quick Backup / New Config actions), the
four MetricCard stat panels, and the two GlassPanels, using the P2 tokens + P3 shared
components (TSMetricCard/TSGlassPanel/TSBadge/TSButton/TSSelect/TSStepper/TSToggle/TSTextField/
TSTextArea/TSEmptyState/TSAlertBanner/TSErrorDisplay/TSSkeleton/TSCard) — no hand-rolled glass.
Adaptive across macOS/iPad (columnar Grid) and iPhone (cards). Every visible string resolves
from Localizable.xcstrings with the web key names (80 keys added). All 13 source files compile
clean under the project's Swift-6 complete-concurrency build; the model + formatters are
harness-verified 45/45. The full xcodebuild scheme is RED ONLY due to two pre-existing,
out-of-scope sibling-file errors (DriveScorePage app source; VehicleCostPageModelTests test)
with ZERO diagnostics in any of my files.

